Cell[TextData[{
 "Statement: a vertex list ",
 StyleBox["A", "TI"],
 " is an antichain when its elements are events of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 ", no event is repeated, and for any two distinct ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["A", "TI"],
 " neither ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " \[PrecedesSlantEqual] ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " nor ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " \[PrecedesSlantEqual] ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 ": no directed path of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " joins them. The empty list and every single event are antichains."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b945169d-34ec-4dec-9a2a-9628b5c5cbc3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An antichain is the discrete form of an achronal set, events no signal can \
connect. It is the opposite of a chain (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraChainQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraChainQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4518338b-ec52-49b1-8990-d9f06062a9e7"],
 "): a chain and an antichain share at most one event. Every slice of the \
height foliation is an antichain (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSliceQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraSliceQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a3a3f84f-42b8-4187-831e-535cdd6f0c5c"],
 " implies it), and so is every subset of an antichain."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a8895367-d104-42d3-a98c-44afa94237e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The width of an order, the size of its largest antichain, equals by \
Dilworth's theorem the least number of chains that cover the events, and is \
the number of events minus a maximum matching of the comparability relation \
(Fulkerson). A sprinkling of ",
 StyleBox["N", "TI"],
 " events into a causal diamond of 1 + 1 Minkowski space is a random \
two-dimensional order, whose width, like its longest chain, grows like 2\
\[Sqrt]",
 StyleBox["N", "TI"],
 " (Ulam's problem)."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6e194ad1-96d6-461f-bb54-3c71d3453b35"]
}, Open  ]],

